<Song resolves-to="SongSP" spName="AngelEyes-G-Theme" spTempo="88">
  <spVERSION>4</spVERSION>
  <spComments>Year:	1946
Composer:	Matt Dennis
Lyricist:	Earl K. Brent
Form:	32-bar AABA
Style:	Torch Ballad
Key:	D minor (often performed in C minor)

“Angel Eyes” was composed by Matt Dennis with
lyrics by Earl K. Brent and was introduced in the 1953
film Jennifer. Some secondary sources give 1941 as
the writing date, but 1946 is the more consistently
documented composition/publication year; the tune’s
original key is generally identified as D minor, though
C minor is common in modern lead sheets and
performances. </spComments>
